@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_Path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Accordion}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Overview_Tests}")]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Accordion @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Overview_Tests</PageTitle>

<section class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Class @GlobalValues.Info_Box_Coloured_Modifier">
    <h1 class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Accordion @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Overview_Tests</h1>

    <p>
        An accordion is a component that displays a list of items where each item has a header (the trigger) and a content panel. Clicking the header toggles 
        the panel open or closed, showing or hiding the content beneath it.
    </p>
    <p>
        <b>Released: </b>Current version <b>v1.0.0</b> See the documentation site for more information: <a target="_blank" class="@GlobalValues.Link_Class" href="@GlobalValues.Site_Link_Docs_Accordion">Accordion documentation (opens in new window)</a>
    </p>
</section>

<section class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Class">

    <h2 class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">Information & instructions</h2>
    <p>
        Below is a single Accordion component which, in this instance has been configured to allow multiple items to be expanded at once as opposed to just one.
        There is also no restriction of having at least one item expanded at all times, all panels can be collapsed.
    </p>
    <p>
        Using the keys as descirbed below, navigate the accordion items ensuring you can expand and collapse a focused accordion item.
    </p>
    <p>
        Each accordion items panel content only contains Lorem Ipsum text without any focusable elements.
    </p>
    <h2 id="tabs-keyboard" class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">Keyboard interaction</h2>
    <ul aria-labelledby="tabs-keyboard">
        <li>
            <kbd>Tab</kbd> - when focus moves into the accordion, places focus onto the the first or last accordion item heading / button.
            <br />When the accordion item is expanded focus moves to the first focusable element within the accordion panel or focus is set on the panel itself. 
            <br />When the accordion item is collapsed focus moves to the next accordion heading or off the accordion going to the next focusable element on the page.
        </li> 
        <li><kbd>Shift + Tab</kbd> reverses tab direction. See above.</li>
        <li><kbd>Up Arrow</kbd> - moves focus to the previous accordion heading. If the focus is on the first heading, moves focus to the last heading.</li> 
        <li><kbd>Down Arrow</kbd> - moves focus to the next accordion heading. If the focus is on the last tab, moves focus to the first heading.</li> 
        <li><kbd>Space or Enter</kbd> - expands or collapses the selected accordion item.</li> 
        <li><kbd>Home</kbd> - moves focus to the first according heading.</li> 
        <li><kbd>End</kbd> - moves focus to the last accordion heading.</li>
    </ul>

</section>
<section class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Class">

    <h3 class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">Expectations</h3>

    <ul>
        <li>
            Tabbing to the Accordion component should set focus on the first accordion heading/button.
        </li>
        <li>
            The up and down arrow keys should move the focus to the previous or next accordion heading, with the home and end keys setting focus to the first or last heading respectively.
        </li>
        <li>
            Using the enter or space key should expand or collapse the accordion items panel. Screen reader users should be advised of the state, expanded/collapsed.
        </li>
        <li>
            As each accordion items panel content has no focusable elements (in this instance), pressing the tab key on a focused heading should set focus to the accordion panel itself.
            Pressing the tab key again should take you to the next focusable element (accordion heading) or out of the accordion to the next focusable element on the page.
        </li>
        <li>
            Voice control users should be able to navigate, expand or collapse accordion items by using the visible accessible name with the associated command, such as focus Food, expand Travel, collapse Exercise.
        </li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="section-box">
    <h3>Accordion test using expand mode multiple</h3>

    <Accordion HeadingLevel="HeadingLevel.H3" ExpandMode="ExpandMode.Multiple">
        <AccordionItem HeadingText="Food" PanelHasTabIndex="true" PanelIsRegion="false" SvgIcon="--svg-food-icon">
            <PanelContent>
                <p>
                    Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Proin sit amet sem vulputate, interdum justo vitae, sagittis nulla. Ut lectus augue, consectetur ut massa id,
                    tristique luctus eros. Donec tempus augue velit, vel vehicula tellus consequat vel. Integer tristique sem ac nisi sodales placerat. Integer nulla ex, tincidunt ut
                    eleifend ut, vestibulum vel leo. Proin diam urna, finibus porttitor purus nec, tristique varius justo. Nunc vel dui sed dui elementum facilisis. Curabitur ac fermentum
                    urna. Integer vestibulum fermentum massa, quis auctor elit viverra eget.
                </p>
            </PanelContent>
        </AccordionItem>
        <AccordionItem HeadingText="Travel" PanelHasTabIndex="true" PanelIsRegion="false" SvgIcon="--svg-airplane-icon">
            <PanelContent>
                <p>
                    Nulla eu est lacus. Mauris sodales tortor in sem viverra porta. Nam in dapibus massa. Vivamus et augue quis mauris luctus pretium eu eu dolor. Maecenas gravida nisl non
                    ante facilisis, pulvinar vestibulum nibh sagittis. Pellentesque mollis sem at arcu mattis, id molestie augue cursus. Pellentesque dolor urna, ultricies quis iaculis ac,
                    rutrum luctus nulla. Integer et consequat erat. Sed eget metus in est pulvinar ultrices at nec lorem. Sed aliquam massa eget dui aliquet ullamcorper. Sed elit nisi, maximus
                    et erat molestie, bibendum rutrum diam. Phasellus cursus eleifend porta.
                </p>
            </PanelContent>
        </AccordionItem>
        <AccordionItem HeadingText="Exercise" PanelHasTabIndex="true" PanelIsRegion="false" SvgIcon="--svg-runner-icon">
            <PanelContent>
                <p>
                    Mauris imperdiet nisi nec pulvinar porta. Sed semper viverra venenatis. Sed accumsan, erat condimentum ornare malesuada, erat mauris tincidunt enim, non interdum quam sem
                    ac velit. Nunc et enim lorem. Maecenas gravida tortor eget ligula efficitur ullamcorper. Cras ut nisi elementum, maximus ante eu, vestibulum nibh. Vestibulum nec iaculis elit,
                    sit amet sagittis ex.
